cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use FlowTrace in published work, please cite it as below."
title: "FlowTrace: a hardware-aware CFD solver and warm-start companion for Ansys Fluent"
abstract: >-
  FlowTrace is an open-source Python CFD solver (incompressible Navier-Stokes,
  Boussinesq energy, RANS turbulence, conjugate heat transfer, moving reference
  frames) that measures the CPU and GPU of the machine it runs on and places
  each stage of the solve where it is fastest. It reads and writes Ansys Fluent
  mesh, case, data and interpolation files, so a FlowTrace solution can
  initialise a Fluent run (warm start).
type: software
authors:
  - name: "mayimhamid"
  - name: "FlowTrace contributors"
license: MIT
version: 0.3.0
date-released: "2026-10-26"
keywords:
  - computational fluid dynamics
  - SIMPLEC
  - RANS
  - GPU computing
  - verification and validation
  - Ansys Fluent interoperability
